<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17714" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">farrāgo</span></b> , ĭnis,
			f.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>mixed fodder for cattle</i>, <i>mash.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Prop.: farrago appellatur
			id, quod ex pluribus satis pabuli causa datur jumentis, Paul. ex
				<i><span class="en">Fest. p. 91, 14</span></i> Müll.; <i><span class="en">Varr.
				R. R. 1, 31, 5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 18, 16, 41, § 142</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Verg.
				G. 3, 205</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Nemes. Cyneg.
			283</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b> * </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>A medley</i>, <i>hodge-podge</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nostri libelli,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Juv. 1,
					86</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>A trifle</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tenuis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Pers.
					5, 77</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
